{#
    A band: the ground runs edge to edge, the content does not.

    The quiet variant is the second ground, with a hairline at each edge, and
    two quiet bands in a row share one. `:rule:` is the line between two
    bands on the same ground.

    The document's nodes stand in the band itself. A box between the two takes
    the band's own rule off them. The last block gives its step up at the edge
    of the band, and a wrapper in between kept it. So every band was one step
    deeper below its content than above it. The heading is plain. The document
    layer is what sets a heading, and a class here is the one `h2` on the page
    that ignores it.
#}
<section class="sds-band{% if node.option('quiet') %} sds-band--quiet{% endif %}{% if node.option('rule') %} sds-band--ruled{% endif %}"
         {%- if node.option('id') %} id="{{ node.option('id') }}"{% endif %}>
    {%- if node.option('title') %}
        <h2>{{ node.option('title') }}</h2>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</section>
